This paper examines the existence of solutions to the following singular double phase problem defined on a bounded open subset $\Omega$ of a complete Riemannian manifold $(M^n,g)$:
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
-\Delta u-\frac{h}{u^{\gamma}}=\lambda u+p(x)u^{\alpha}\text{ in }\Omega,\\
u>0\text{ in }\Omega,\\
u=0\text{ on }\partial\Omega,
\end{cases}
\end{cases}
where $h\geq 0$, $\gamma>2$, and the operator $\Delta$ represents the Laplace-Beltrami operator associated with $g$. The function $p$ is a given nonnegative function, while the operator $\Delta$ is governed by the generalized double phase functional
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\mathcal{F}(u)=\int_M\left(|\nabla u|^{p(x)}+A(x)|u|^{q(x)}\right)dx,\\
&\text{with }1<\gamma<q\leq p\text{ being variable exponents satisfying the critical Sobolev growth condition.}
\end{split}
\end{equation}
